Improved: SolverCG now runs a pipelined variant of the conjugate gradient
method for LinearAlgebra::distributed::Vector with MemorySpace::Default when
the preconditioner is PreconditionIdentity or a DiagonalMatrix. All vector
updates of an iteration are fused into a single device kernel before the
matrix-vector product, and all inner products into a single kernel after it.
This needs only one global reduction per iteration instead of three, reduces
the number of kernel calls by design, and reduces the memory access.
<br>
(Martin Kronbichler, 2026/11/24)
